# Implementation Plan: Distributed Real-Time Events (MongoDB Change Streams / Hybrid Fallback)

To support scaling the platform to 600+ concurrent employees and multiple PM2 cluster processes, we must ensure real-time events (like new inquiries arriving) are propagated across all processes. 

We will transition the SSE system to a **Hybrid MongoDB Change Streams** implementation with an **in-memory EventEmitter fallback**.

## Proposed Changes

### Real-Time Infrastructure

#### [NEW] [inquiry-events-dist.ts](file:///c:/TV/insurance-platform/lib/inquiry-events-dist.ts)
- Implement a distributed event manager that listens to MongoDB Change Streams (`Inquiry.watch()`) for new documents.
- If MongoDB is running in standalone mode (no Replica Set configured), capture the error and fallback gracefully to the in-memory `EventEmitter`.

#### [MODIFY] [route.ts](file:///c:/TV/insurance-platform/app/api/inquiries/stream/route.ts)
- Update the GET endpoint to subscribe to the new distributed event manager.

#### [MODIFY] [route.ts](file:///c:/TV/insurance-platform/app/api/inquiries/route.ts)
- Ensure all created inquiries publish to the distributed event manager so fallback clients receive them.

